=head1 DESCRIPTION

A list of the user attributes and their properties in your user pool.
The attribute schema contains standard attributes, custom attributes
with a C<custom:> prefix, and developer attributes with a C<dev:>
prefix. For more information, see User pool attributes
(https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/user-pool-settings-attributes.html).

Developer-only C<dev:> attributes are a legacy feature of user pools,
and are read-only to all app clients. You can create and update
developer-only attributes only with IAM-authenticated API operations.
Use app client read/write permissions instead.

=head1 ATTRIBUTES


=head2 AttributeDataType => Str

The data format of the values for your attribute. When you choose an
C<AttributeDataType>, Amazon Cognito validates the input against the
data type. A custom attribute value in your user's ID token is always a
string, for example C<"custom:isMember" : "true"> or
C<"custom:YearsAsMember" : "12">.


=head2 DeveloperOnlyAttribute => Bool

You should use WriteAttributes
(https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito-user-identity-pools/latest/APIReference/API_UserPoolClientType.html#CognitoUserPools-Type-UserPoolClientType-WriteAttributes)
in the user pool client to control how attributes can be mutated for
new use cases instead of using C<DeveloperOnlyAttribute>.

Specifies whether the attribute type is developer only. This attribute
can only be modified by an administrator. Users won't be able to modify
this attribute using their access token. For example,
C<DeveloperOnlyAttribute> can be modified using
AdminUpdateUserAttributes but can't be updated using
UpdateUserAttributes.


=head2 Mutable => Bool

Specifies whether the value of the attribute can be changed.

Any user pool attribute whose value you map from an IdP attribute must
be mutable, with a parameter value of C<true>. Amazon Cognito updates
mapped attributes when users sign in to your application through an
IdP. If an attribute is immutable, Amazon Cognito throws an error when
it attempts to update the attribute. For more information, see
Specifying Identity Provider Attribute Mappings for Your User Pool
(https://docs.aws.amazon.com/cognito/latest/developerguide/cognito-user-pools-specifying-attribute-mapping.html).


=head2 Name => Str

The name of your user pool attribute. When you create or update a user
pool, adding a schema attribute creates a custom or developer-only
attribute. When you add an attribute with a C<Name> value of
C<MyAttribute>, Amazon Cognito creates the custom attribute
C<custom:MyAttribute>. When C<DeveloperOnlyAttribute> is C<true>,
Amazon Cognito creates your attribute as C<dev:MyAttribute>. In an
operation that describes a user pool, Amazon Cognito returns this value
as C<value> for standard attributes, C<custom:value> for custom
attributes, and C<dev:value> for developer-only attributes..


